# Phase 0 manual spike — VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP client / `httpie`.
# Goal: prove we can read tank + battery and start climatisation on Nico's own
# car, and measure token lifetimes. See ../../RESEARCH.md "Phase 0".
#
# Fill these after creating the Volvo app + doing one browser OAuth by hand.

@apiKey = PUT_VCC_API_KEY_HERE
@accessToken = PUT_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@vin = PUT_VIN_HERE
@base = https://api.volvocars.com

### API backend status (no auth)
GET https://public-developer-portal-bff.weu-prod.ecpaz.volvocars.biz/api/v1/backend-status

### List vehicles on the consented Volvo ID
GET {{base}}/connected-vehicle/v2/vehicles
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
vcc-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### Fuel  (tank % / litres + distance to empty)
GET {{base}}/connected-vehicle/v2/vehicles/{{vin}}/fuel
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
vcc-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### Energy state  (battery %, charging, electric range, time-to-full)
GET {{base}}/energy/v2/vehicles/{{vin}}/state
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
vcc-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### Statistics  (distanceToEmptyTank / distanceToEmptyBattery, trip meters)
GET {{base}}/connected-vehicle/v2/vehicles/{{vin}}/statistics
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
vcc-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### Odometer
GET {{base}}/connected-vehicle/v2/vehicles/{{vin}}/odometer
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
vcc-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### Doors (+ carLocked) / Windows / Diagnostics
GET {{base}}/connected-vehicle/v2/vehicles/{{vin}}/doors
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
vcc-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

###
GET {{base}}/connected-vehicle/v2/vehicles/{{vin}}/windows
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
vcc-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

###
GET {{base}}/connected-vehicle/v2/vehicles/{{vin}}/diagnostics
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
vcc-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### Which commands does this VIN support / is it reachable now
GET {{base}}/connected-vehicle/v2/vehicles/{{vin}}/commands
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
vcc-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

###
GET {{base}}/connected-vehicle/v2/vehicles/{{vin}}/command-accessibility
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
vcc-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### >>> RELEASE 1 COMMAND: start climatisation (default scope) <<<
POST {{base}}/connected-vehicle/v2/vehicles/{{vin}}/commands/climatization-start
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
vcc-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### stop climatisation
POST {{base}}/connected-vehicle/v2/vehicles/{{vin}}/commands/climatization-stop
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
vcc-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### RESTRICTED SCOPE probe — does the test env allow these without a separate request?
POST {{base}}/connected-vehicle/v2/vehicles/{{vin}}/commands/flash
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
vcc-api-key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Refresh token — run repeatedly over days to learn the real refresh-token lifetime
# @clientId / @clientSecret basic-auth; body is form-encoded
POST https://volvoid.eu.volvocars.com/as/token.oauth2
Authorization: Basic {{clientId}} {{clientSecret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token=PUT_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE
